        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Community Counts: Friends of the Teton River</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/50046.webp" alt="Community Counts: Friends of the Teton River" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>For twenty years, <a href="https://www.tetonwater.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Friends of the Teton River</a><a href="https://cfjh.iphiview.com/cfjh/DonorView/AccountInformation/tabid/495/dispatch/accountselection_id$10960_hash$b8fbafd594c2b0c7c707af450c9d41817a9e92db/Default.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"> </a>(FTR) has worked with local partners on projects to improve water resources through practical, community-focused solutions. Thanks to a best-in-class staff, dedicated partners, and our committed and generous benefactors, we have been able to realize tremendous success in river and stream conservation, collaborative conservation, community education, cutting-edge fisheries research, and native fish restoration. Together with you, we have made things happen that seemed like impossible dreams when we began in 2001.</p>

<p>Building on this legacy and expanding our positive impact takes commitment and focus.&nbsp;&nbsp;It takes science, creative thinking, and the ability to build trust and strong partnerships across groups that sometimes see each other as problems rather than solutions.&nbsp;&nbsp;It takes our committed and generous community, who shares these values.&nbsp;</p>

<p>With a clear vision, we enter the next two decades poised to create even more lasting impact. The core of our mission is to implement practical on-the-ground solutions to improve our watershed with and for our community. This year, your Tin Cup gift will help support priority projects that have been developed with local partners that:</p>

<ul><li><strong>Expand habitat for native cutthroat trout.</strong>&nbsp;FTR and irrigation partners are restoring flow and connecting habitat in the vast Canyon Creek drainage for spawning native cutthroat trout.<strong></strong></li><li><strong>Restore streams and reduce flood risk.&nbsp;</strong>We are working with homeowners, landowners, and local government to restore healthy stream function on Teton Creek and the upper Teton River.&nbsp;<strong></strong></li><li><strong>Increase water availability.&nbsp;</strong>Our aquifer recharge and irrigation infrastructure improvement efforts increase water availability and flows for people and fish.&nbsp;<strong></strong></li><li><strong>Connect with stakeholders.&nbsp;</strong>We bring together scientists, farmers, anglers, and community members to build collaborative, on-the-ground solutions to watershed issues in a changing climate.<strong></strong></li><li><strong>Promote stewardship.</strong>&nbsp;We are working with local government, state agencies, businesses, and river users to create a community-driven plan for responsible Teton River recreation and stewardship.<strong></strong></li></ul>

<p>We are excited about what lies ahead. We are confident that we will continue to build upon our first twenty years, and that the return on your investment – in our watershed and our work – will continue to grow year after year, creating a legacy of clean water, healthy streams, and a thriving wild fishery that outlasts us all.</p>

